# OnboardAGV — register an AGV with the master so MQTT messages from
# this AGV are routed to handlers. Wraps VDA5050Master::onboard_agv.
# Service half of Task #53.
#
# **Idempotency**: re-onboarding the same {manufacturer, serial_number}
# returns ALREADY_ONBOARDED without disturbing the existing AGV
# instance. FMS clients can call this safely on every startup or on
# AGV-pool addition.
#
# **What onboarding does master-side**:
#   - Creates an AGV instance with a per-AGV ProtocolAdapter.
#   - Subscribes to the AGV's MQTT topics (state, connection,
#     factsheet, visualization).
#   - Adds the AGV to the master's onboarded list (visible to other
#     services like AssignOrder, GetDeviceStatus, etc.).
#
# Optional ctor params `max_queue_size` and `drop_oldest` are exposed
# with the same defaults as the C++ signature; FMS clients that don't
# care can omit them and accept defaults.

string manufacturer
string serial_number

# AGV outbound message-queue capacity. 0 means "use master default" (10).
uint32 max_queue_size 0

# Queue-full policy. true (default) drops oldest message; false rejects
# the new message. Distinct from max_queue_size==0 sentinel — applies
# even under the default queue size.
bool drop_oldest true
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS              — AGV successfully onboarded; master will start
#                        routing MQTT messages from this AGV.
# ALREADY_ONBOARDED    — an AGV with this {manufacturer, serial_number}
#                        is already in the master's onboard list.
#                        Idempotent no-op; treat as success — the
#                        existing AGV instance is untouched.
# INVALID_REQUEST      — empty manufacturer or serial_number.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 ALREADY_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 status

# Echo of request — async-fanout correlation.
string manufacturer
string serial_number
